{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121705","id":4121666129,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc71q6JR","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121705","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121705.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121705.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121705","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121705/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121705/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121705/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/726bcdf70562937e224ccc94a9654eb272d0f347","number":121705,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix TextEdit.get_rect_at_line_column()","user":{"login":"BrotherShort","id":129957860,"node_id":"U_kgDOB77_5A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/129957860?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrotherShort","html_url":"https://github.com/BrotherShort","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrotherShort/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrotherShort/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrotherShort/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrotherShort/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrotherShort/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrotherShort/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrotherShort/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrotherShort/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrotherShort/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fix #121704\r\n\r\n---\r\nI modified the failing unit test, because I believed the unit test was incorrect.\r\nThe comment states, “Select to the first character of a wrapped line.” However, the unit test actually selected the last character of the previous line.\r\nThe test previously passed because it relied on an incorrect result returned by the `get_rect_at_line_column()`.\r\n\r\nThe screen corresponding to the unit test:\r\n<img width=\"167\" height=\"139\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0e11996c-c2b6-40c3-8da7-f6f2c402240e\" />\r\n---\r\nNote:\r\nCaret columns start at 0; char columns start at 1. \r\n<img width=\"762\" height=\"761\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f71a053c-2c75-45b4-99c4-f042deb0e57d\" />\r\nThe `wrap_index` of the char at col 1 equals the `wrap_index` of the caret at col 0. \r\nSo, I need to pass `p_column - 1` to `get_line_wrap_index_at_column`.\r\n\r\nThe valid values for `get_rect_at_line_column`'s `p_column` is 1<=`p_column`<= line length. So, the range of values for `p_column - 1` is 0<=`p_column - 1`<= line length-1.\r\nBut in fact, the `get_rect_at_line_column` can accept 0, and the return result is the same as when 1 is passed.\r\nIf `p_column` is 0, `p_column - 1` will be `-1`. Should we perform parameter validation to convert -1 to 0? It’s optional.\r\nIf we pass -1 to `get_line_wrap_index_at_column`, it will not cause errors but return 0 directly.\r\nOf course, we can also choose to add parameter checks to improve robustness.\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1732720779,"node_id":"MDU6TGFi